    "https://www.geneseo.edu/provost/prodig-plus/": {
      "title": "PRODiG+ Fellowship Opportunity",
      "description": "PRODiG+ Fellowship Opportunity - SUNY Geneseo Skip to content Search this site About About Facts Campus Map Awards & Rankings Diversity News Center Directory Meet Our Faculty Academics Academics Schools and Departments Majors, Minors, and Academic Programs Research Study Abroad Career Design Center Library Admissions Office of Admissions Visit and Connect Apply First Year Transfer Graduate International Tuition And Aid Campus Life Campus Life Clubs and Organizations Events Calendar Residential Communities Dining & Catering Info For Future Students Current Students Faculty And Staff Alumni Parents and Families Community Members Athletics Give Apply Apply Search this site Apply Apply Office of the Provost Provost Office Staff Academic Affairs Divisional Structure Academic Affairs Leadership Teams Distinguished and Award-Winning Faculty and Staff Recent Faculty & Staff Milestones Sabbatical and Other Leaves Academic Affairs Awards Academic Affairs News Academic Affairs Racial Justice Initiatives Applying for Faculty Positions PRODiG+ Fellowship Opportunity Geneseo Curriculum League of Storytellers Workforce Development Contact Us About About Facts Campus Map Awards & Rankings Diversity News Center Directory Meet Our Faculty Academics Academics Schools and Departments Majors, Minors, and Academic Programs Research Study Abroad Career Design Center Library Admissions Office of Admissions Visit and Connect Apply First Year Transfer Graduate International Tuition And Aid Campus Life Campus Life Clubs and Organizations Events Calendar Residential Communities Dining & Catering Info For Future Students Current Students Faculty And Staff Alumni Parents and Families Community Members Athletics Give Home Office of the Provost PRODiG+ Fellowship Opportunity Office of the Provost Provost Office Staff Academic Affairs Divisional Structure Academic Affairs Leadership Teams Distinguished and Award-Winning Faculty and Staff Recent Faculty & Staff Milestones Sabbatical and Other Leaves Academic Affairs Awards Academic Affairs News Academic Affairs Racial Justice Initiatives Applying for Faculty Positions PRODiG+ Fellowship Opportunity Geneseo Curriculum League of Storytellers Workforce Development Contact Us PRODiG+ Fellowship Opportunity SUNY Geneseo is pleased to participate in the Promoting Recruitment, Opportunity, Diversity, Inclusion and Growth Plus (PRODiG+) program designed to focus on two goals: (1) increasing the number and share of excellent diverse faculty committed to advancing the ideals of diversity, equity, and inclusion; and (2) strengthening the pipeline for retention and support of these candidates. Fellowship Eligibility To participate in PRODiG+, candidates will be required to: Be eligible to work in the United States without a visa sponsorship; Have a PhD or relevant terminal degree from an accredited institution completed prior to start date; and Demonstrate personal, academic, and/or work experience engaging with diversity, equity, and inclusion and/or a commitment to facilitating and enhancing diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Such experience may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record incorporating diversity, equity, and inclusion; work (paid/unpaid) or volunteer/community service; and/or related experience in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations. Fellows are welcome to focus on a wide range of scholarly topics and disciplinary areas, emphasizing promoting and impacting diversity, equity, and inclusion through scholarship, teaching, and service to the campus community. Preference will be given to candidates who are: Current SUNY students, alumni, and/or Fellows. From a low-income background (e.g., Pell-eligible as undergraduates), were first-generation college students (students whose parents have not earned a bachelor’s degree), have overcome adversity, are AmeriCorps alumni, or are veterans. The PRODiG+ Fellowship is open to any and all prospective candidates regardless of race, color, national origin, or sex, and is consistent with all current governing federal and state nondiscrimination law. All application submissions will be assessed and evaluated in accordance with the required eligibility criteria. Questions about the program may be addressed to provost@geneseo.edu . Quick Links Contact Geneseo Campus Map Directory Emergency Info Quick Links Contact Geneseo Campus Map Directory Emergency Info Join Us Apply to Geneseo Transfer to Geneseo Alumni Community Work at Geneseo Join Us Apply to Geneseo Transfer to Geneseo Alumni Community Work at Geneseo Policies Title IX Policy and Reporting Form Anti-Hazing Policy and Reporting Form Policies Title IX Policy and Reporting Form Anti-Hazing Policy and Reporting Form Website Info Accessibility Privacy Student Right to Know Web Editor Login Website Info Accessibility Privacy Student Right to Know Web Editor Login Copyright © 2026 SUNY Geneseo Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Bluesky YouTube Scroll to Top"
    },
